      "credit": "Own work by the original uploader",
      "source": "Ostia gate",
      "description": "Inscription from one of the gates of the Roman port of Ostia Antica. According to an interpretation by F. Zevi (1998) the latin inscription reads: SENATVS POPVLVSQVE ROMANVSCOLONIAE OSTIENSIVM MVROS ET PORTAS DEDITM. TVLLIVS CICERO CO(n)S(ul) FECIT CVRAVITQUE[?]P. CLODIVS PVLCHER TR(ibunus) PL(ebis) CONSVMMAVIT ET PROBAVITPORTAM VETVSTATE CORRVPTAM [...]\n This can be loosely translated as: \"The senate of Rome gave Ostia these walls and gates, constructed under the guidance of Consul M. Tullius Cicero, completed by Tribune P. Clodius Pulcher, which had long been ruined.\"",
